  "worked_solution": "Starting from the definition of the Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{-8t}m(t)} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{-8t}\\,m(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s+8)t}\\,m(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $M(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,m(t)\\,\\text{d}t,$ where $s>{s}_{0}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s+8)t}\\,m(t)\\,\\text{d}t=M(s+8),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\ns+8>{s}_{0}\\,\u21d2\\,s>{s}_{0}-8.\n$$",
